      "message": "From [this screenshot](https://screenshot.googleplex.com/BkbcT4Abq2LMiJb), I see an example, `^::drawCount\u003d1`.\n\n`^` is probably helpful - it tells us that this slice is associated with the one above.\n\n`::` seems weird - I tend to think of this symbol as denoting a class member. I was thinking maybe we could use parentheses? These are parameters to the macro, after all.\n\n`\u003d` - i might have a small preference for `: ` instead, but I think this is fine.",
